            <ArticleTitle>Coronary vasospasm: a neuro-behavioral event?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>369-74</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Evidence exists for the presence of a neuro-anatomy that can produce cardiac vasospasm. Recent experimental and clinical data suggest that this neuro-anatomic mechanism can be activated by behavioral events in the psycho-social surround of the patient with coronary artery disease. I hypothesize that this mechanism can produce myocardial ischemia and can explain the variability in onset of clinical angina.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
